    <statement><p>Use a CAS to calculate <m>\int_{\mathcal{C}} \left\lt  e^{x-y},e^{x+y} \right&gt;\cdot \,d\mathbf{\,s}</m> to four decimal places,</p>
<p>where <m>\mathcal{C}</m> is the curve <m>y=\sin x</m> for
<m>0\le x \le \frac{\pi}{5}</m>, oriented from left to right.</p>
<p>Answer: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1.76965</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\mathbf{c}(t) = \left\lt  t, \sin t \right&gt;</m>,
our integral becomes
<me>\int_0^{\frac{\pi}{5}} \left\lt  e^{t-\sin t},e^{t+\sin t}\right&gt; \cdot \left\lt  1, \cos t \right&gt; \, dt</me>
Which is calculated to be <m>1.76965</m>.



</solution>
